00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:26.000
All right.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:29.000
Forgive us while we transition here for just a moment.

00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:33.000
But, as I'm sure you've already either heard when you arrived

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:35.000
or if you were late into the building,

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:37.000
we have some new faces on the stage tonight,

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:39.000
or some different faces, I should say,

00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:41.000
because it's Youth Sunday.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:46.000
Yay! Yes! Right? That's awesome.

00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:51.000
And I'm so excited.

00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:54.000
I'm so proud of them.

00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:58.000
I just, there are a few things that I look forward to more

00:26:58.000 --> 00:27:02.000
than seeing these students who oftentimes you guys don't get to see

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:05.000
because they're back serving in our kids' ministry area every week,

00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:10.000
in classrooms, or, you know, like they're in here on a rotation

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:12.000
because they're back there serving,

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:15.000
or after the service they're back in the youth room.

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:20.000
And to see them be part of this community,

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:24.000
not just as someone who is served, but someone who is serving,

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:27.000
and using their gifts, and knowing that what they have

00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:30.000
is good enough to make a difference and to bless people.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:38.000
And I am one of those kids who had so many grown-ups in their lives

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:41.000
saying, you have something to offer.

00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:46.000
And I was never, ever, ever even allowed to be on the back row.

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:49.000
I mean, not because it was like this rule.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:52.000
It was just from the beginning I was invited into the front lines

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:54.000
of whatever was happening.

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:57.000
And I'm so thankful that I was raised in a community like that.

00:27:57.000 --> 00:28:00.000
It literally changed my life.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.000
I mean, majorly.

00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:07.000
So as soon as we were doing anything related to church planting,

00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:10.000
the first thing I was looking for was the students

00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:12.000
because I was one of those kids.

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:14.000
That's where it started for me,

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:17.000
was as a little 7th grade girl with my crazy youth pastor

00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:19.000
coming up to me and being like,

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:22.000
hey, you want to start leading worship every Wednesday night at our, you know,

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:24.000
and I didn't know what I was doing.

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:31.000
And it turned into a lifelong, just fulfilling invitation into ministry.

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:33.000
So I hope that happens for them.

00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:36.000
And I'm just proud of them for saying yes.

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:38.000
So the three people you see in front of you tonight

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:41.000
have agreed to be part of our message portion of the service.

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:46.000
And Hank Humble is going to be kind of our point guy.

00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:49.000
And, yes.

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:52.000
Hank is skilled and talented in a thousand ways.

00:28:52.000 --> 00:28:54.000
A thousand ways, y'all.

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:56.000
He's so dang gifted.

00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:58.000
It's unreal.

00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:02.000
And I'm just really excited that you get to hear from him tonight.

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:05.000
And Maylynn is next to him.

00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:07.000
And Maylynn, yes.

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:09.000
Give Maylynn a hand.

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:12.000
Maylynn is a junior at Sac State High School.

00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:19.000
And this is like the most upfront thing that Maylynn maybe has ever done

00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:21.000
in their whole entire life.

00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:23.000
So I'm like beaming with pride already,

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:25.000
and nothing's even come out of your mouth yet.

00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:29.000
Just them sitting here right now is like, yes, victory!

00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:32.000
No one forced you into it, though, right?

00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:33.000
Yeah.

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:35.000
This is like a major step of courage.

00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:38.000
And then this is Chloe Kaiser next to me.

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:42.000
And you guys already got to hear a little bit from her.

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:44.000
But hopefully you'll get to know them a little bit better.

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:46.000
And we're going to just be talking and sharing some of the things

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:51.000
that we've been focusing on in youth since the beginning of the year in January.

00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:54.000
And I'm going to kick it over to you guys.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:56.000
Hank, are you good on that mic?

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:57.000
I think so.

00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:58.000
Test, test.

00:29:58.000 --> 00:29:59.000
Okay.

00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:01.000
I'll put this one down then.

00:30:01.000 --> 00:30:02.000
All right.

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:03.000
Good evening, everybody.

00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:04.000
How's it going?

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:05.000
Let's see.

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:06.000
Everybody make the turnout.

00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:08.000
So my name is Hank.

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:10.000
I am 17 years old.

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:12.000
My pronouns are he, him.

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:17.000
And tonight we're going to be talking about just stuff we've been going over in youth.

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:20.000
And we have a few questions too.

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:21.000
So I'll take it to you all.

00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:25.000
What is your name and your pronouns?

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:26.000
Hello.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:27.000
I'm Maylynn.

00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:31.000
And my pronouns, I go by Annie.

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:35.000
I'm Chloe, and I go by she, her.

00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:36.000
Awesome.

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:37.000
All right.

00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:40.000
So we are part of the youth.

00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:42.000
We are a pretty fun bunch.

00:30:42.000 --> 00:30:43.000
Next slide, please.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:44.000
Yeah.

00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:46.000
So you can see we've got some pictures up.

00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:48.000
We hang out, have snacks, play games.

00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:53.000
It's usually about like 6.15, 6.30 to 8.

00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:59.000
And if we schedule well enough, sometimes we even do some Bible study at the end of our talk.

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:02.000
But, yeah, it's a really fun time to just kind of reflect.

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:05.000
It's a really safe space for me especially.

00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:12.000
I've felt like I've been able to vent and just share the things that have been heavy on my mind.

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:16.000
It's one of my favorite times of the week.

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:19.000
So next slide, please.

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:27.000
The themes we've been going over recently are kind of awareness, just being more connected to those around you,

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:34.000
personal ownership and owning up to your own shortcomings, realizing that we're all flawed in some way,

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:42.000
and just being more understanding, just being a cool, chill guy, you know, being a well-rounded individual.

00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:44.000
Next slide, please.

00:31:44.000 --> 00:31:49.000
With that, we've been also going over the Enneagram a lot lately.

00:31:49.000 --> 00:31:55.000
Some people are kind of like, oh, that's like the astrology, whatever, pseudoscience.

00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:58.000
Well, but it's a lot more like a personal compass.

00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:04.000
It's a really useful tool for being better aided to learn more about those around you,

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:11.000
understanding yourself, and just, yeah, being a good person.

00:32:12.000 --> 00:32:16.000
Not a good person, but, you know.

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:23.000
With that in mind, it's kind of just the idea of primary strengths and flaws within ourselves,

00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:31.000
and we all have our own kind of like centric driving force.

00:32:31.000 --> 00:32:33.000
They break it up into three.

00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:37.000
It's the two, three, and four are the heart center.

00:32:37.000 --> 00:32:43.000
The body center is eight, nine, and one, and the mind is five, six, and seven.

00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:53.000
I usually kind of lead towards heart, but really we all have a little bit of each type within us,

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:57.000
but one has kind of pushed to the top over time.

00:32:57.000 --> 00:32:59.000
And not everybody has a type.

00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:01.000
Usually children don't really have types.

00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:08.000
It kind of is something that develops more once you've matured a little bit.

00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:13.000
I personally am an Enneagram type four.

00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:19.000
It's kind of the angsty one.

00:33:19.000 --> 00:33:22.000
I'm kind of in my motions right now.

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:28.000
They say a lot about it being like trying to understand a sense of self,

00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:34.000
but it's also kind of feels like there's something missing a lot of the time,

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:42.000
or like people don't try to connect more with people, but maybe they don't quite get it.

00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:49.000
So like at their best, you can see on the left side, we're authentic people.

00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:54.000
We wear our colors, but in our worst, we're hopeless.

00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:56.000
It's just terrible.

00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:59.000
So with that in mind, I'll take it over to our panel.

00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:06.000
My question is what is your Enneagram type, and what does it mean to you?

00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:11.000
Okay, so I am a type nine with a wing one.

00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:18.000
Type nine is a peacemaker, meaning I strive for harmony and peace,

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:22.000
not only in my environment, but with myself.

00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:27.000
Our fears are afraid of disconnection.

00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:32.000
So like that, yeah, definitely.

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:37.000
We are known as doormats in the nicest way possible.

00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:39.000
We're doormats.

00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:43.000
We allow people to do things to us in order to keep the peace,

00:34:43.000 --> 00:34:49.000
in order to just keep things the same, which is our weakness.

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:53.000
We are conflict avoidant and too accepting, also very indecisive,

00:34:53.000 --> 00:34:58.000
which if you know me, yeah, it will be the downfall of me

00:34:58.000 --> 00:35:03.000
because I cannot choose anything for the life of me.

00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:12.000
But we are also known to be easygoing, receptive, reassuring, and self-effacing,

00:35:12.000 --> 00:35:19.000
meaning we don't claim attention.

00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:22.000
And the wing one is called the dreamer.

00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:29.000
So they are – it's pretty much just the same.

00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:34.000
But when they're doing bad, they don't take risks.

00:35:34.000 --> 00:35:37.000
I mean like that's why they're called the dreamer

00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:49.000
because they don't take risks in fear of, like, well.

00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:51.000
Sorry.

00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:54.000
No, you're doing great.

00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:56.000
Are you ready to move on?

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.000
Well, thank you for sharing, Maylin.

00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:01.000
And Chloe, we'd love to hear from you next.

00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:04.000
I am a three, which is the achiever.

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:08.000
So I kind of like – I really like to keep my image

00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:11.000
and I'm always trying to be achieving something.

00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:14.000
I always like to be on the go looking for the next thing.

00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:17.000
I find it very hard to fail or to be bad at anything.

00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:20.000
And if somebody is better at something than me,

00:36:20.000 --> 00:36:24.000
I find that very difficult to get over.

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:27.000
I really long to feel valuable and worthwhile,

00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:31.000
like I'm worthy of being somewhere or that people see me as.

00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:33.000
Not necessarily like they like to be around me,

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:35.000
but like that girl, she's on it.

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:38.000
She's got everything figured out.

00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:42.000
So I have a really big fear of being worthless,

00:36:42.000 --> 00:36:48.000
just like people being like, what's she doing over there?

00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:51.000
So I see myself as very image conscious

00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:55.000
and impatient and competitive and that's kind of my downfalls.

00:36:55.000 --> 00:36:57.000
Once I get something figured out, I'm kind of like,

00:36:57.000 --> 00:36:59.000
well, why can't you figure this out too?

00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:04.000
I don't want to wait for you to catch up to me.

00:37:04.000 --> 00:37:08.000
So sometimes it's hard for me to decide what's more important,

00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:11.000
like God's opinions, like over my grain,

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:14.000
like if I get a worse grade on a friend than something

00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:17.000
or even if I do better but I don't get the perfect score,

00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:20.000
I'm like, well, it's easy for me to feel proud of others,

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:25.000
but I'm just like, well, those are five or ten points that you missed,

00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:27.000
so you're still a failure.

00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:32.000
So it's definitely been having to have some come to Jesus moments

00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:36.000
of being like, your worth does not come from how you perform,

00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:38.000
it comes from God.

00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:39.000
So, yeah.

00:37:39.000 --> 00:37:40.000
Thank you, Chloe.

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:42.000
That was wonderful.

00:37:42.000 --> 00:37:46.000
So one of the other key themes we've been kind of discussing

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:49.000
and just one of the key values at the church as a whole

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:54.000
is the idea of eclecticism, the being eclectic.

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:57.000
The Webster Dictionary over here describes it as

00:37:57.000 --> 00:38:03.000
deriving ideas, styles, or tastes from a broad and diverse range of sources.

00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:07.000
So, yeah, eclectic mix of courses.

00:38:10.000 --> 00:38:13.000
I included this in the slide to kind of give us a chance to share

00:38:13.000 --> 00:38:16.000
just some fun little things we like talking about,

00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:18.000
but my question for everybody is,

00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:21.000
what are some things in life that you've found God in

00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:23.000
or that have given you peace and faith?

00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:25.000
So I'll share first.

00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:31.000
Some things that have been really driving for me recently

00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:35.000
are I've found some new friends within my school.

00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:42.000
As a 4, it's been hard for me to find good friends,

00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:47.000
but church has been a good home for me,

00:38:47.000 --> 00:38:51.000
but also needing to kind of out in the rest of the world.

00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:56.000
I've recently found a good group of friends who are my main supporters.

00:38:56.000 --> 00:39:00.000
They've been my main crew,

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:03.000
and it's been really nice to be able to just vent

00:39:03.000 --> 00:39:06.000
and hang out and have a good time.

00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:12.000
I've also developed a little bit of a green thumb myself lately.

00:39:12.000 --> 00:39:14.000
It's been...

00:39:14.000 --> 00:39:18.000
I've kind of seen it in a perspective of...

00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:20.000
I've found faith in it,

00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:27.000
from feeling it like it's taking God's gifts and sources from the earth

00:39:27.000 --> 00:39:29.000
and being able to cultivate it.

00:39:29.000 --> 00:39:32.000
It just kind of makes my heart feel good.

00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:34.000
Seeing the plants grow, I'm like,

00:39:34.000 --> 00:39:36.000
I'm doing it, but it's God doing it.

00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:38.000
Like, what is...

00:39:38.000 --> 00:39:42.000
And I've also had this little Mr. Rogers calendar

00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:46.000
that stays up above my desk on this little bookshelf,

00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:50.000
but it always has a little quote of wisdom,

00:39:50.000 --> 00:39:52.000
inspiration in the mornings,

00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:54.000
and they're really nice.

00:39:54.000 --> 00:39:58.000
And this blue one up here kind of relates to what we've been talking about,

00:39:58.000 --> 00:40:01.000
of there's the good guy and the bad guy in all of us,

00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:04.000
and knowing that doesn't ever need to overwhelm us.

00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:07.000
Or when we value childhood and the many things children can do,

00:40:07.000 --> 00:40:11.000
we're letting them know that we don't expect them to be more grown-ups

00:40:11.000 --> 00:40:13.000
than they're already ready to be.

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:15.000
We like them just the way they are.

00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:16.000
Yeah.

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:19.000
So with that in mind, the question for each of you is,

00:40:19.000 --> 00:40:22.000
what are some things in life that you've found God in,

00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:24.000
or given you peace and faith?

00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:28.000
So one of the things I find God in is...

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:31.000
Oh, my name's spelled wrong.

00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:34.000
It's okay. It's okay.

00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:36.000
Is art.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:39.000
My life is very chaotic,

00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:41.000
especially with my family,

00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:45.000
and being a junior halfway through the school year

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:48.000
where you're getting ready to look for colleges and everything,

00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:51.000
it's just, like, chaotic.

00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:55.000
So art gives me a chance to just, you know, simmer down,

00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:58.000
just not really think about things,

00:40:58.000 --> 00:41:02.000
and it just allows me to just think about, like,

00:41:02.000 --> 00:41:05.000
my relationship with God.

00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:09.000
And then kids' ministry, or, well, my nieces,

00:41:09.000 --> 00:41:11.000
who are in the middle, those little goofballs.

00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:14.000
If you knew me, if you know me,

00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:17.000
you know that there's, like, not a day that goes by

00:41:17.000 --> 00:41:21.000
where I don't bring them up in some way,

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:23.000
or show you pictures.

00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:27.000
I know some of you are probably tired of that.

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:31.000
But I see God in children, especially them.

00:41:31.000 --> 00:41:34.000
They are so, like, lively,

00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:37.000
and they're so innocent,

00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:40.000
and you can just, like, see them

00:41:40.000 --> 00:41:42.000
just going about and learning things,

00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:45.000
and it's just, like, so amazing.

00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:49.000
And then I put Perks of Being a Wallflower,

00:41:49.000 --> 00:41:51.000
which is an amazing movie.

00:41:51.000 --> 00:41:53.000
Very sad.

00:41:53.000 --> 00:41:56.000
Not for many people.

00:41:56.000 --> 00:42:00.000
But I resonate with the main character, Charlie,

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:03.000
who is a freshman in high school

00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:06.000
and a very awkward, very lonely person.

00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:08.000
He went through a lot of traumatic stuff,

00:42:08.000 --> 00:42:13.000
like losing his friend and going through sexual abuse.

00:42:15.000 --> 00:42:17.000
So I really resonate with him,

00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:22.000
because it's just, like, he is messed up in the first part.

00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:25.000
And the whole movie is just him

00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:29.000
learning to make friends and be healthier.

00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:33.000
And he does mess up, like, in the last part of the movie.

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:36.000
He goes through a lot.

00:42:36.000 --> 00:42:41.000
And one of the quotes in the movie is,

00:42:41.000 --> 00:42:44.000
we accept the love we think we deserve,

00:42:44.000 --> 00:42:48.000
which is insanely true on my half,

00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:50.000
especially being a peacemaker.

00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:53.000
I just let people do things to me,

00:42:53.000 --> 00:42:56.000
because I think either I think I deserve it,

00:42:56.000 --> 00:43:00.000
or I just, like, don't want to hurt anyone

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:02.000
or don't want to make things worse.

00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:04.000
So I just let them do it,

00:43:04.000 --> 00:43:08.000
which is not healthy, and I'm trying to get better with that.

00:43:08.000 --> 00:43:14.000
I also see many people in my life getting hurt by people

00:43:14.000 --> 00:43:17.000
because they think they deserve that.

00:43:17.000 --> 00:43:20.000
They don't know that they deserve more than that,

00:43:20.000 --> 00:43:22.000
and it hurts a lot.

00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:27.000
But at the end of the movie, he ends up finding friends,

00:43:27.000 --> 00:43:29.000
which is what I'm getting better with.

00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:32.000
I have amazing people in my life,

00:43:32.000 --> 00:43:35.000
not just in kids' ministry, I mean kids' ministry,

00:43:35.000 --> 00:43:38.000
in youth group, but in school.

00:43:38.000 --> 00:43:41.000
I've had friends who I really, like, connect with

00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:47.000
who have helped me, like, get a healthier mindset

00:43:47.000 --> 00:43:51.000
and, like, just strive for a healthier life.

00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:53.000
Thank you for that insight, Malin.

00:43:53.000 --> 00:43:55.000
That was wonderful.

00:43:55.000 --> 00:43:57.000
And, Chloe, we'd love to hear from you next.

00:43:57.000 --> 00:43:59.000
Yes.

00:43:59.000 --> 00:44:03.000
So a few things that, a lot of it comes from the shows

00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:05.000
I've been watching lately,

00:44:05.000 --> 00:44:08.000
which is, the first one is Modern Family,

00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:12.000
or more specifically, The Mom, named Claire.

00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:14.000
And if you don't know this show,

00:44:14.000 --> 00:44:17.000
Claire is, like, the mom of three,

00:44:17.000 --> 00:44:20.000
and she has kind of an incompetent husband.

00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:25.000
And she's, like, she's very controlling and competitive

00:44:25.000 --> 00:44:27.000
and driven, and she gets really impatient.

00:44:27.000 --> 00:44:30.000
And I'm, like, as soon as I saw the first episode,

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:33.000
I was, like, I think God is sending me this show

00:44:33.000 --> 00:44:36.000
and this woman to grow along with her.

00:44:36.000 --> 00:44:38.000
And in this one episode,

00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:40.000
this is literally the episode I was thinking about,

00:44:40.000 --> 00:44:42.000
Hank got it exactly right.

00:44:42.000 --> 00:44:44.000
It was, like, Claire has something done to her

00:44:44.000 --> 00:44:47.000
by her husband, and while Claire is, like,

00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:50.000
you guys, I'm right, I know I'm right, he did this.

00:44:50.000 --> 00:44:52.000
And her husband's, like, no, I didn't.

00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:55.000
And I can just see the pain in her face.

00:44:55.000 --> 00:44:58.000
She is, like, he did it, I'm right, I know it.

00:44:58.000 --> 00:45:02.000
And she goes to crazy lengths to prove that she is right.

00:45:02.000 --> 00:45:05.000
And when her kids find out that she is right in the end,

00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:07.000
and what she did to prove herself,

00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:11.000
they're, like, are you sick, are you okay, are you crazy?

00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:14.000
And I was just, like, you know,

00:45:14.000 --> 00:45:16.000
maybe sometimes I can step back, too.

00:45:16.000 --> 00:45:19.000
And so, as she grows, I just feel

00:45:20.000 --> 00:45:22.000
God calling me to grow along with her.

00:45:22.000 --> 00:45:26.000
And then that second show there is called Severance.

00:45:26.000 --> 00:45:30.000
I've been watching this show with my family recently.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:33.000
And for those who don't know it, it's kind of complex,

00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:36.000
but I'll try to, like, sum it up really quick.

00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:38.000
It follows this group of coworkers

00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:41.000
whose brains have been, like, surgically divided.

00:45:41.000 --> 00:45:44.000
So they don't know, like, they go home,

00:45:44.000 --> 00:45:46.000
and they know who they are,

00:45:46.000 --> 00:45:49.000
but they don't know what they do at work, and vice versa.

00:45:49.000 --> 00:45:52.000
And so there's one character named Helena,

00:45:52.000 --> 00:45:54.000
and I resonate deeply with, like,

00:45:54.000 --> 00:45:57.000
both parts of her innie and her outie.

00:45:57.000 --> 00:46:03.000
So her outie is very composed and driven and confident,

00:46:03.000 --> 00:46:06.000
and she's always, like, not trying to lose her patience

00:46:06.000 --> 00:46:09.000
or, like, just trying to prove that she's worth where she's at,

00:46:09.000 --> 00:46:12.000
which is how I feel a lot of the time when I'm at school,

00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:15.000
like, constantly trying to feel like I am enough,

00:46:15.000 --> 00:46:17.000
I am worthy to be where I am at,

00:46:17.000 --> 00:46:20.000
and just trying to be patient and calm and keeping my mouth shut.

00:46:20.000 --> 00:46:23.000
But then outside of school, I feel like her innie,

00:46:23.000 --> 00:46:26.000
or who she is, like, at work,

00:46:26.000 --> 00:46:30.000
and she's fierce and controlling and independent and impatient

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:33.000
and speaks her mind and unrelenting.

00:46:33.000 --> 00:46:36.000
And so at this stage in my life,

00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:40.000
I kind of feel God calling me to find, like,

00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:43.000
the balance between these Helenas, like, in my own world

00:46:43.000 --> 00:46:45.000
and, like, speak my mind,

00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:48.000
but also be someone who knows when to back down

00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:51.000
and just listen and observe,

00:46:51.000 --> 00:46:55.000
but also feel, like, my inside Hellie

00:46:55.000 --> 00:46:57.000
and, like, not doubt my worth

00:46:57.000 --> 00:47:00.000
and be able to just speak my mind.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:05.000
And so my last thing is this song called Everything's in Your Hands.

00:47:05.000 --> 00:47:07.000
And so throughout this year,

00:47:07.000 --> 00:47:10.000
and it being my first year in high school,

00:47:10.000 --> 00:47:13.000
I find it very easy to go to school

00:47:13.000 --> 00:47:15.000
and have the mindset of you're going to do the best

00:47:15.000 --> 00:47:17.000
or you're going to fail.

00:47:17.000 --> 00:47:19.000
There's no gray area.

00:47:19.000 --> 00:47:21.000
There's no in between.

00:47:21.000 --> 00:47:23.000
And so it's really easy to feel like as a three,

00:47:23.000 --> 00:47:25.000
my worth is in my performance.

00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:29.000
And so whenever I have a stressful test the next day

00:47:29.000 --> 00:47:33.000
or I'm about to do, like, a performance for a band or something,

00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:35.000
this song is just kind of like,

00:47:35.000 --> 00:47:38.000
this song is, like, it's for God.

00:47:38.000 --> 00:47:40.000
It's not, at the end of the day,

00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:43.000
nothing determines your worth except God

00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:45.000
and what you're doing is for God

00:47:45.000 --> 00:47:48.000
and all of your power just comes from Him.

00:47:48.000 --> 00:47:51.000
So, yeah, this song has just kind of been able to keep me grounded

00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:54.000
and steady and guide me forward.

00:47:54.000 --> 00:47:55.000
So, yeah.

00:47:55.000 --> 00:47:57.000
That's beautiful, Chloe.

00:47:57.000 --> 00:47:59.000
It really is a good song.

00:47:59.000 --> 00:48:01.000
Thank you for sharing.

00:48:01.000 --> 00:48:04.000
So moving along, we have also,

00:48:04.000 --> 00:48:07.000
one of the main passages we've been following

00:48:07.000 --> 00:48:10.000
is Galatians 6, 1 through 5.

00:48:10.000 --> 00:48:14.000
Maggie has actually been a really big promoter of this one.

00:48:14.000 --> 00:48:16.000
She's been sharing it a lot with me lately.

00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:22.000
And I realized when I was, like, flipping through my Bible I was given here,

00:48:22.000 --> 00:48:24.000
when I was looking it up,

00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:26.000
I noticed it was highlighted in pink and said,

00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:28.000
this one.

00:48:28.000 --> 00:48:30.000
Yeah.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:33.000
So let me share it with you all.

00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:36.000
Brothers and sisters, if someone is caught in a sin,

00:48:36.000 --> 00:48:39.000
you who live by the Spirit should restore that person gently.

00:48:39.000 --> 00:48:42.000
But watch yourselves, or you also may be tempted.

00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:44.000
Carry each other's burdens,

00:48:44.000 --> 00:48:47.000
and in this way you will fulfill the law of Christ.

00:48:47.000 --> 00:48:49.000
If anyone thinks they are something when they are not,

00:48:49.000 --> 00:48:51.000
they deceive themselves.

00:48:51.000 --> 00:48:53.000
Each one should test their own actions,

00:48:53.000 --> 00:48:56.000
and they take pride in themselves alone,

00:48:56.000 --> 00:48:58.000
without comparing themselves to someone else,

00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:01.000
for each one should carry their own load.

00:49:01.000 --> 00:49:03.000
So it's interesting.

00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:05.000
There's a lot going on here.

00:49:05.000 --> 00:49:14.000
I really like how it kind of brings up topics of the self-dictating

00:49:14.000 --> 00:49:17.000
and being more accountable,

00:49:17.000 --> 00:49:21.000
but also watching out for your fellow neighbor

00:49:21.000 --> 00:49:27.000
and just reaching out a more gracious, kind hand.

00:49:27.000 --> 00:49:29.000
So with this in mind,

00:49:29.000 --> 00:49:34.000
the question I've kind of posed to kind of wrap us up

00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:37.000
is what has this season of life been like for you,

00:49:37.000 --> 00:49:41.000
and how have you seen your faith in God play a role in your journey?

00:49:41.000 --> 00:49:47.000
So I'll share first.

00:49:47.000 --> 00:49:51.000
2025 has been good but hard, hard.

00:49:51.000 --> 00:49:54.000
I've been wrapping up my school year,

00:49:54.000 --> 00:50:01.000
and time just feels so, so fleeting, so precious.

00:50:01.000 --> 00:50:06.000
I have a summer internship option that might come up for me,

00:50:06.000 --> 00:50:10.000
but I'm still waiting for them to give me the message back.

00:50:10.000 --> 00:50:13.000
So there's been a lot of longing, too,

00:50:13.000 --> 00:50:15.000
because it's a whole summer away,

00:50:15.000 --> 00:50:17.000
and I have three younger siblings.

00:50:17.000 --> 00:50:19.000
These are like the precious moments.

00:50:19.000 --> 00:50:20.000
They're losing teeth.

00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:22.000
They're learning life lessons.

00:50:22.000 --> 00:50:25.000
My little sister just learned how to ride a bike like two days ago.

00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:28.000
So it's like, oh, I'm going to come back,

00:50:28.000 --> 00:50:31.000
and they're going to be taller than me.

00:50:31.000 --> 00:50:35.000
They're still my little siblings,

00:50:35.000 --> 00:50:38.000
so I'm still able to get mad at them sometimes,

00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:40.000
but they do feel like my kids half the time.

00:50:40.000 --> 00:50:44.000
So it's just a lot of heavy stuff,

00:50:44.000 --> 00:50:47.000
realizing how quickly things are moving.

00:50:47.000 --> 00:50:50.000
So I've been trying to kind of, as much as I can,

00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:52.000
kind of center myself again,

00:50:52.000 --> 00:50:55.000
kind of slowing it down with things like reading,

00:50:55.000 --> 00:50:57.000
more intentional prayer.

00:50:57.000 --> 00:51:00.000
I've been trying to avoid prayer in bed,

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:02.000
where I'm just kind of thinking,

00:51:02.000 --> 00:51:05.000
and more like before I go to bed,

00:51:05.000 --> 00:51:07.000
I usually lay out my yoga mat

00:51:07.000 --> 00:51:10.000
and kind of actually get on my knees and pray.

00:51:10.000 --> 00:51:13.000
I've noticed it kind of really feels like

00:51:13.000 --> 00:51:16.000
more manifesting my relationship with God,

00:51:16.000 --> 00:51:19.000
because I've always felt that kind of disconnect.

00:51:19.000 --> 00:51:21.000
Like it's just like, I'm just thinking about God,

00:51:21.000 --> 00:51:24.000
but when I'm actually like, God,

00:51:24.000 --> 00:51:27.000
it feels a lot more real.

00:51:27.000 --> 00:51:31.000
So I found some ways to kind of slow it down

00:51:31.000 --> 00:51:33.000
and reel in the peace.

00:51:33.000 --> 00:51:36.000
So with that in mind, I'd like to ask each of y'all,

00:51:36.000 --> 00:51:38.000
what has this season of life been like for you,

00:51:38.000 --> 00:51:40.000
and have you seen your faith in God

00:51:40.000 --> 00:51:42.000
play a role in your journey?

00:51:42.000 --> 00:51:46.000
Okay, so my life could be, like this year,

00:51:46.000 --> 00:51:49.000
it could be explained as a roller coaster,

00:51:49.000 --> 00:51:52.000
which is ironic, because I'm terrified of roller coasters,

00:51:52.000 --> 00:51:54.000
I just don't like heights.

00:51:54.000 --> 00:51:57.000
But there's been good days

00:51:57.000 --> 00:51:59.000
where I'm just like happy to be here,

00:51:59.000 --> 00:52:02.000
I am excited to do things,

00:52:02.000 --> 00:52:05.000
and then there's other days where I just struggle

00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:08.000
to do the simple tasks, like getting up in the morning,

00:52:08.000 --> 00:52:11.000
or like just taking a shower,

00:52:11.000 --> 00:52:14.000
which, if you know me, I have to take a shower every day.

00:52:14.000 --> 00:52:17.000
Every day, it's, yeah.

00:52:17.000 --> 00:52:21.000
But it's just like some days,

00:52:21.000 --> 00:52:24.000
I just can't find myself to do it.

00:52:24.000 --> 00:52:26.000
But I have to force myself,

00:52:26.000 --> 00:52:30.000
because life does not stop even if you're feeling bad.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:37.000
But recently, I've been taking medication for my anxiety,

00:52:37.000 --> 00:52:39.000
which has been helping a lot,

00:52:39.000 --> 00:52:42.000
and hopefully in the near future,

00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:44.000
I will be finding therapy,

00:52:44.000 --> 00:52:47.000
which should be very soon.

00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:51.000
And I'm glad I have people I could talk to,

00:52:51.000 --> 00:52:53.000
because if it wasn't for that,

00:52:53.000 --> 00:52:55.000
I don't know where I would be today.

00:52:57.000 --> 00:53:00.000
Sorry, I just got better from a cold.

00:53:02.000 --> 00:53:05.000
And it's a lot,

00:53:05.000 --> 00:53:07.000
especially like starting to look into colleges,

00:53:07.000 --> 00:53:09.000
I am very stressed.

00:53:10.000 --> 00:53:14.000
If you did not know that, I am very stressed.

00:53:14.000 --> 00:53:18.000
But I have been looking more into finding God.

00:53:18.000 --> 00:53:22.000
I was never really like religious-religious.

00:53:22.000 --> 00:53:24.000
I grew up in a Catholic household

00:53:24.000 --> 00:53:27.000
where everyone believed in God,

00:53:27.000 --> 00:53:28.000
and they were practicing,

00:53:28.000 --> 00:53:31.000
but I just didn't know where I stood in that.

00:53:31.000 --> 00:53:32.000
I would go to church,

00:53:32.000 --> 00:53:35.000
but I wouldn't take in the messages.

00:53:35.000 --> 00:53:38.000
I wouldn't really understand what was the meaning.

00:53:38.000 --> 00:53:42.000
But now I've been like trying to get more aware,

00:53:42.000 --> 00:53:44.000
and I've been trying to connect myself,

00:53:44.000 --> 00:53:46.000
which sometimes is really hard,

00:53:46.000 --> 00:53:49.000
because something bad happens to you,

00:53:49.000 --> 00:53:51.000
and you're like, why me?

00:53:51.000 --> 00:53:56.000
Why did you put this obstacle in my path?

00:53:57.000 --> 00:53:59.000
But then you realize

00:53:59.000 --> 00:54:01.000
that it's just to make you a better person.

00:54:01.000 --> 00:54:05.000
It's to somewhat test you,

00:54:05.000 --> 00:54:08.000
because God tests his people.

00:54:08.000 --> 00:54:14.000
He tests people for the better.

00:54:18.000 --> 00:54:20.000
I don't know what else to say.

00:54:20.000 --> 00:54:22.000
Thank you for sharing.

00:54:22.000 --> 00:54:23.000
Chloe?

00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:25.000
So this year,

00:54:25.000 --> 00:54:29.000
it's more like stretching into the 24-25 school year.

00:54:29.000 --> 00:54:32.000
This has been my first year of high school,

00:54:32.000 --> 00:54:34.000
which is automatically already terrifying,

00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:38.000
but this was less of like the ideal,

00:54:38.000 --> 00:54:40.000
like not ideal,

00:54:40.000 --> 00:54:42.000
but like stereotypical high school experience,

00:54:42.000 --> 00:54:45.000
and more of just like having to figure out

00:54:45.000 --> 00:54:47.000
how to manage 12-15 hour days,

00:54:47.000 --> 00:54:49.000
and higher expectations,

00:54:49.000 --> 00:54:51.000
and how grades actually count,

00:54:51.000 --> 00:54:53.000
and just new forms of anxiety

00:54:53.000 --> 00:54:56.000
that I never thought I would have to feel.

00:54:56.000 --> 00:54:58.000
And like this was the first year,

00:54:58.000 --> 00:54:59.000
like as a three,

00:54:59.000 --> 00:55:01.000
most things come easily to me,

00:55:01.000 --> 00:55:03.000
and I vividly remember sitting down,

00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:04.000
and my mom was like,

00:55:04.000 --> 00:55:05.000
you know,

00:55:05.000 --> 00:55:06.000
Chloe,

00:55:06.000 --> 00:55:07.000
this might be the first year

00:55:07.000 --> 00:55:08.000
that you're actually going to have to try

00:55:08.000 --> 00:55:09.000
and work for things,

00:55:09.000 --> 00:55:10.000
you know,

00:55:10.000 --> 00:55:11.000
harder than you used to.

00:55:11.000 --> 00:55:12.000
And I was like,

00:55:12.000 --> 00:55:13.000
yep,

00:55:13.000 --> 00:55:14.000
yep,

00:55:14.000 --> 00:55:15.000
figured that out pretty quick.

00:55:15.000 --> 00:55:19.000
And so I feel a lot like

00:55:19.000 --> 00:55:23.000
my faith has grown a lot stronger through this,

00:55:23.000 --> 00:55:27.000
and it feels like I've only like

00:55:27.000 --> 00:55:29.000
needed more of God in my life

00:55:29.000 --> 00:55:30.000
outside of church,

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:33.000
and tried to like not just be here

00:55:33.000 --> 00:55:35.000
for this hour-long service,

00:55:35.000 --> 00:55:37.000
but to also bring him home,

00:55:37.000 --> 00:55:38.000
and like talk to him.

00:55:38.000 --> 00:55:40.000
And me and my family have this little term

00:55:40.000 --> 00:55:41.000
for Sunday nights

00:55:41.000 --> 00:55:43.000
before going into a school week,

00:55:43.000 --> 00:55:45.000
which is Sunday Scaries,

00:55:45.000 --> 00:55:46.000
and so I'll just be like

00:55:46.000 --> 00:55:48.000
lying in bed on Sunday night,

00:55:48.000 --> 00:55:50.000
and I'm just like freaking out,

00:55:50.000 --> 00:55:51.000
and I'm like,

00:55:51.000 --> 00:55:52.000
I'll just start praying,

00:55:52.000 --> 00:55:53.000
and I'm like,

00:55:53.000 --> 00:55:54.000
God,

00:55:54.000 --> 00:55:55.000
I'm pretty scared, man.

00:55:55.000 --> 00:55:56.000
I don't know what to do.

00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:57.000
There's a lot of tests this week.

00:55:57.000 --> 00:55:58.000
I don't know what I'm going to do.

00:55:58.000 --> 00:55:59.000
If I fail,

00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:00.000
I don't know what's going to happen.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:01.000
Will the grades tank?

00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:03.000
Like, will this one week affect

00:56:03.000 --> 00:56:04.000
what colleges I get into?

00:56:04.000 --> 00:56:06.000
And then I'll just be like,

00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:09.000
no, it's okay.

00:56:09.000 --> 00:56:11.000
And so,

00:56:11.000 --> 00:56:13.000
as well as praying more,

00:56:13.000 --> 00:56:16.000
I find that sometimes when I pray,

00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:17.000
I put it off until like

00:56:17.000 --> 00:56:18.000
the very last second at night,

00:56:18.000 --> 00:56:19.000
and then I'll be like,

00:56:19.000 --> 00:56:21.000
dear God,

00:56:21.000 --> 00:56:23.000
and then just fall asleep,

00:56:23.000 --> 00:56:24.000
and it doesn't happen.

00:56:24.000 --> 00:56:25.000
And so what I found is

00:56:25.000 --> 00:56:27.000
I start like,

00:56:27.000 --> 00:56:28.000
I've always journaled,

00:56:28.000 --> 00:56:29.000
but it's kind of like

00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:30.000
meaningless journaling,

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:31.000
and so this year,

00:56:31.000 --> 00:56:32.000
I've started like journaling

00:56:32.000 --> 00:56:34.000
like with a set purpose,

00:56:34.000 --> 00:56:35.000
and I start everything with like,

00:56:35.000 --> 00:56:37.000
dear Jesus,

00:56:37.000 --> 00:56:38.000
and it's like I'm writing

00:56:38.000 --> 00:56:39.000
a letter to him almost,

00:56:39.000 --> 00:56:41.000
saying what I'm worrying about,

00:56:41.000 --> 00:56:42.000
and then just kind of

00:56:42.000 --> 00:56:43.000
sending that off

00:56:43.000 --> 00:56:44.000
and releasing my worries

00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:45.000
along with it,

00:56:45.000 --> 00:56:46.000
which has been really helpful,

00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:49.000
so I'm excited to keep

00:56:49.000 --> 00:56:50.000
growing my relationship

00:56:50.000 --> 00:56:52.000
and becoming a better version

00:56:52.000 --> 00:56:53.000
of myself.

00:56:53.000 --> 00:56:55.000
Yes.

00:56:55.000 --> 00:56:57.000
Thank you so much.

00:56:58.000 --> 00:57:00.000
Well, thank you.

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:02.000
As we wrap up tonight,

00:57:02.000 --> 00:57:03.000
this is kind of a question

00:57:03.000 --> 00:57:05.000
for all the audience.

00:57:05.000 --> 00:57:06.000
I encourage you to reflect

00:57:06.000 --> 00:57:07.000
on your own journey.

00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:08.000
Where do you need

00:57:08.000 --> 00:57:10.000
accountability?

00:57:10.000 --> 00:57:11.000
How can you be more aware

00:57:11.000 --> 00:57:12.000
of your own strengths

00:57:12.000 --> 00:57:13.000
and weaknesses?

00:57:13.000 --> 00:57:14.000
How can you better support

00:57:14.000 --> 00:57:16.000
and encourage those around you?

00:57:16.000 --> 00:57:17.000
Let's be gentle with another,

00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:19.000
but also firm in our commitment

00:57:19.000 --> 00:57:20.000
to growth.

00:57:20.000 --> 00:57:21.000
It's been really nice

00:57:21.000 --> 00:57:23.000
to share with all of y'all

00:57:23.000 --> 00:57:25.000
how life's been like for us,

00:57:25.000 --> 00:57:27.000
what's on our minds.

00:57:27.000 --> 00:57:28.000
So I think I might end off

00:57:28.000 --> 00:57:29.000
with a quick little

00:57:29.000 --> 00:57:31.000
impromptu prayer.

00:57:33.000 --> 00:57:35.000
All right.

00:57:35.000 --> 00:57:36.000
Dear Lord,

00:57:36.000 --> 00:57:37.000
thank you for this evening.

00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:38.000
Thank you that we

00:57:38.000 --> 00:57:39.000
have the opportunity

00:57:39.000 --> 00:57:41.000
to share how we're,

00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:42.000
what's on our minds,

00:57:42.000 --> 00:57:43.000
how we're feeling

00:57:43.000 --> 00:57:45.000
with the church.

00:57:45.000 --> 00:57:46.000
Thank you that we could hear

00:57:46.000 --> 00:57:49.000
from these wonderful people,

00:57:49.000 --> 00:57:50.000
all the cool hip ideas

00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:52.000
we got going,

00:57:52.000 --> 00:57:55.000
and please guide us

00:57:55.000 --> 00:57:57.000
with your strength in mind

00:57:57.000 --> 00:57:59.000
and your grace

00:57:59.000 --> 00:58:01.000
and unconditional love

00:58:01.000 --> 00:58:03.000
guiding us in every decision

00:58:03.000 --> 00:58:05.000
we make in the future.

00:58:05.000 --> 00:58:07.000
Amen.

00:58:08.000 --> 00:58:09.000
All right.

00:58:09.000 --> 00:58:10.000
Thank you for,

00:58:10.000 --> 00:58:11.000
thank you for listening

00:58:11.000 --> 00:58:13.000
to us yap up here.

00:58:13.000 --> 00:58:15.000
Thank you.

00:58:44.000 --> 00:58:46.000
So what we do,

00:58:46.000 --> 00:58:47.000
I think most of y'all

00:58:47.000 --> 00:58:48.000
know the drill,

00:58:48.000 --> 00:58:49.000
but what we do here

00:58:49.000 --> 00:58:51.000
is we practice

00:58:51.000 --> 00:58:53.000
what's called an open table.

00:58:53.000 --> 00:58:55.000
So even if your

00:58:55.000 --> 00:58:56.000
faith alignments

00:58:56.000 --> 00:58:58.000
aren't quite in tune yet

00:58:58.000 --> 00:59:00.000
or you feel on the rocks

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:02.000
about certain things,

00:59:02.000 --> 00:59:04.000
we, within faith

00:59:04.000 --> 00:59:05.000
and everything,

00:59:05.000 --> 00:59:06.000
we still invite you

00:59:06.000 --> 00:59:08.000
to come up and partake

00:59:08.000 --> 00:59:10.000
with communion this evening.

00:59:10.000 --> 00:59:12.000
So this is the Celtic call.

00:59:12.000 --> 00:59:14.000
This is the,

00:59:14.000 --> 00:59:15.000
this is the table,

00:59:15.000 --> 00:59:16.000
not of the church,

00:59:16.000 --> 00:59:17.000
but of the Lord.

00:59:17.000 --> 00:59:18.000
It's made ready

00:59:18.000 --> 00:59:19.000
for those who love him

00:59:19.000 --> 00:59:20.000
and those who want

00:59:20.000 --> 00:59:21.000
to love him more.

00:59:21.000 --> 00:59:22.000
So come.

00:59:22.000 --> 00:59:23.000
You who have much faith

00:59:23.000 --> 00:59:24.000
and you who have little,

00:59:24.000 --> 00:59:26.000
you who have been here often

00:59:26.000 --> 00:59:27.000
and you who have not,

